    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0538" n="1372" xml:id="pg1372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659a.119/14</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-29T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8006. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 585. Referring further your 626, Embassy 10185, May 22, 5 p.m. We await
                    authorizing your adherence to agreement pending receipt of full text thereof. We
                    do not understand the proposals as to oil contracts, in view of discussions with
                    the British which are proceeding here regarding allotments to companies in
                    accordance with pre-war business.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d432-f1"/> Please cable
                    more fully in regard to apparent exclusion of Standard Oil Company which we
                    understand has heretofore done practically all of the business in Iceland.</p>
                <p>With reference to wool, we will take all wool obtainable provided this can be
                    secured at current United States option prices. Bigelow is familiar with this.
                    We will also take any amount of sheep skins at prices not exceeding the maximum
                    here which is 14 cents per foot New York, c.i.f.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
